# The query library published as a FeatureServer table (layer 1).
#
# This file is the architecture in miniature: the service exposes exactly two
# generic operations, and both of them are the standard ArcGIS `query`.
#
#   1. Discover  -> FeatureServer/1/query   "what can I ask?"
#   2. Execute   -> FeatureServer/0/query   "answer this, using the parameters row 1 gave me"
#
# Adding an analytical question adds a row to table 1. No new endpoint, no new DTO,
# no deployment of the client.
#
# Start the server first: `npm start`.

@svc   = http://127.0.0.1:3000/arcgis/rest/services/ServiceRequests/FeatureServer
@cat   = {{svc}}/1
@layer = {{svc}}/0

### The service advertises one layer and one table
GET {{svc}}?f=pjson

### Table 1 definition — type "Table", no geometry, no extent, no timeInfo
GET {{cat}}?f=pjson

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. DISCOVER — the catalog is an ordinary queryable table
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### The whole catalog (what a dashboard loads on start-up)
GET {{cat}}/query?f=pjson&where=1=1&outFields=QueryNumber,Category,Question,Portability,Transforms&orderByFields=QueryNumber

### Only the questions that run unchanged on any FeatureServer
GET {{cat}}/query?f=pjson&where=Portability = 'standard'&outFields=QueryNumber,Question&orderByFields=QueryNumber

### Only the performance metrics (a category dropdown, server-side)
GET {{cat}}/query?f=pjson&where=Category LIKE '%Duration%'&outFields=QueryNumber,Question,Portability&orderByFields=QueryNumber

### Free-text search across questions and their SQL — no search endpoint needed
GET {{cat}}/query?f=pjson&where=Question LIKE '%percentile%' OR SqlText LIKE '%PERCENTILE_CONT%'&outFields=QueryNumber,Question

### The distinct categories, for a dropdown
GET {{cat}}/query?f=pjson&where=1=1&outFields=Category&returnDistinctValues=true&orderByFields=Category

### The catalog describing itself: how portable is the library?
GET {{cat}}/query?f=pjson&where=1=1&groupByFieldsForStatistics=Portability&outStatistics=[{"statisticType":"count","onStatisticField":"ObjectID","outStatisticFieldName":"Count"}]&orderByFields=Count DESC

### Coverage by 5W+H dimension and analytical layer
GET {{cat}}/query?f=pjson&where=1=1&groupByFieldsForStatistics=AnalyticLayer,Dimension&outStatistics=[{"statisticType":"count","onStatisticField":"ObjectID","outStatisticFieldName":"Count"}]&orderByFields=AnalyticLayer,Count DESC

### How many questions REST cannot finish on its own (they carry a client transform)
GET {{cat}}/query?f=pjson&where=Transforms IS NOT NULL&outFields=QueryNumber,Question,Transforms&orderByFields=QueryNumber

### One row in full — this is everything a client needs to run Q22
GET {{cat}}/query?f=pjson&where=QueryNumber = 22&outFields=*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. EXECUTE — replay the RestParams the catalog just handed over
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The request below was not written by hand: every parameter is copied verbatim
# out of the RestParams column of Q22 above. That is the whole claim.

### Q22 "Average resolution time by Category", executed from its catalog row
POST {{layer}}/query
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

f=pjson
&where=DtCompleted IS NOT NULL
&sqlFormat=native
&groupByFieldsForStatistics=Category
&outStatistics=[{"statisticType":"avg","onStatisticField":"DATEDIFF(day, DtLogged, DtCompleted)","outStatisticFieldName":"AvgDays"}]
&orderByFields=AvgDays

### Q53 "90th percentile resolution time" — the metric that usually needs a new endpoint
POST {{layer}}/query
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

f=pjson
&where=DtCompleted IS NOT NULL
&sqlFormat=native
&outStatistics=[{"statisticType":"percentile_cont","onStatisticField":"DATEDIFF(day, DtLogged, DtCompleted)","outStatisticFieldName":"P90_Days","statisticParameters":{"value":0.9}}]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. The audit trail
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### The reference T-SQL for the same question, served from the same table
GET {{cat}}/query?f=pjson&where=QueryNumber = 22&outFields=QueryNumber,Question,SqlText

### And run it, via the mock's raw-SQL extension (NOT part of ArcGIS REST)
POST {{layer}}/sql
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

f=pjson
&q=SELECT Category, AVG(CAST(DATEDIFF(day, DtLogged, DtCompleted) AS FLOAT)) AS AvgDays FROM ServiceRequest WHERE DtCompleted IS NOT NULL GROUP BY Category ORDER BY AvgDays;

### The catalog is also a view for the raw-SQL extension, mirroring vw_QueryLibrary
POST {{layer}}/sql
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

f=pjson
&q=SELECT Portability, COUNT(*) AS Count FROM QueryLibrary GROUP BY Portability ORDER BY Count DESC;

### Read-only: the catalog cannot be edited over the wire
POST {{layer}}/sql
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

f=pjson
&q=UPDATE QueryLibrary SET Question = 'nope' WHERE QueryNumber = 1;
